  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: The Only Formula You Need -->
  <section id="formula" class="content-section">
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-info">
        <h2>The Only Formula You Need</h2>
        <p>
          Every conversion on this site reduces to one single relationship: the <strong>nano</strong> prefix is <code>10⁻⁹</code> and the <strong>micro</strong> prefix is <code>10⁻⁶</code>. That means one micro is exactly 1,000 times larger than one nano — everywhere, in every unit.
        </p>

        <div class="formula-box gold-box">
          <code>micro = nano ÷ 1,000</code>
        </div>

        <div class="formula-box blue-box">
          <code>nano = micro × 1,000</code>
        </div>

        <p class="muted-note">
          To convert from nanometers to micrometers, divide by 1,000: <strong>2,500 nm ÷ 1,000 = 2.5 µm</strong>. To go the other way, multiply by 1,000: <strong>0.75 µg × 1,000 = 750 ng</strong>. No exceptions, no quirks.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="table-card">
        <h3 class="table-card-title">Nano to Micro Quick Table</h3>
        <table class="quick-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Nano (n)</th>
              <th>Micro (µ)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
